@startuml Germany_Trailer_Rules
!theme plain
skinparam defaultFontSize 12

title Germany — Trailer Rules: Complete Exam Reference (StVO / StVZO)\nCompanion to: stvo_trailer_flowchart.puml (load dimensions and cargo compliance)

start

' ══════════════════════════════════════════════
' STEP 1 — LICENCE CLASS
' ══════════════════════════════════════════════
:STEP 1 — What licence class do I need to tow?;

if (Trailer weight ≤ 750 kg\nAND combined total ≤ 3,500 kg?) then (YES)
  #LightGreen:Class B sufficient
  No extension needed;
else (NO)
  if (Combined total between 3,500 kg and 4,250 kg?) then (YES)
    #Yellow:Class B96 required
    Extension to standard Class B;
  else (NO — combined > 4,250 kg)
    if (Vehicle ≤ 3,500 kg AND trailer ≤ 3,500 kg\nAND combined ≤ 7,000 kg?) then (YES)
      #Orange:Class BE required;
    else (NO)
      #Pink:Higher licence class required
      (Class C / CE — beyond standard car licence);
    endif
  endif
endif

' ══════════════════════════════════════════════
' STEP 2 — SPEED LIMITS
' ══════════════════════════════════════════════
:STEP 2 — What speed limits apply to my combination?;

if (Towing vehicle permissible mass > 3.5 t?) then (YES)
  :**Urban: 50 km/h | Rural: 60 km/h | Autobahn: 80 km/h**
  Trucks > 3.5 t / Motorhomes > 3.5 t / Buses + trailer;
else (NO — towing vehicle ≤ 3.5 t)
  if (Tempo-100 certification obtained?) then (YES)
    #LightGreen:**Urban: 50 km/h | Rural: 80 km/h | Autobahn: 100 km/h**
    Tempo-100 applies on Autobahn and Kraftfahrstraße ONLY
    Rural Bundesstraße (non-expressway) remains 80 km/h;
  else (NO)
    :**Urban: 50 km/h | Rural: 80 km/h | Autobahn: 80 km/h**;
  endif
endif

' ══════════════════════════════════════════════
' STEP 3 — TEMPO-100 ELIGIBILITY
' ══════════════════════════════════════════════
:STEP 3 — Is my trailer eligible for Tempo-100?;

if (Trailer has brakes + shock absorbers\n+ approved anti-sway coupling device?) then (YES)
  #LightGreen:ELIGIBLE — Tempo-100 permitted
  Max trailer weight = car empty weight × **1.2**
  (Caravans and touring trailers);
elseif (Trailer has brakes + shock absorbers\n(no anti-sway coupling)?) then (YES)
  #LightGreen:ELIGIBLE — Tempo-100 permitted
  Max trailer weight = car empty weight × **1.1**
  (Standard braked trailer with shock absorbers);
else (Unbraked OR braked without shock absorbers)
  #Pink:NOT eligible for Tempo-100
  Max trailer weight = car empty weight × **0.3**
  Maximum 80 km/h on all road types;
endif

note right
  Tempo-100 sticker must be affixed
  visibly inside the vehicle (e.g. dashboard).
  Without sticker: 80 km/h limit applies
  even if trailer meets weight ratio.
end note

' ══════════════════════════════════════════════
' STEP 4 — FOLLOWING DISTANCE
' ══════════════════════════════════════════════
:STEP 4 — Following distance rules;

if (Total combination length > 7 metres?) then (YES)
  #Yellow:**Minimum 50 metres following distance required**
  On roads outside built-up areas
  with only one lane per direction.
  Purpose: allow overtaking vehicles to pull in
  safely IN FRONT of your combination.
  (Gap must be sufficient at the FRONT — not behind you);
else (NO — combination ≤ 7 m)
  :Standard following distance rules apply;
endif

' ══════════════════════════════════════════════
' STEP 5 — TRAILER SNAKING (Schlingern)
' ══════════════════════════════════════════════
:STEP 5 — Trailer begins to snake / sway (Schlingern);

#Pink:**DO NOT brake sharply**
**DO NOT accelerate**
Ease off the accelerator gently and smoothly.
Hold the steering wheel firmly — do not steer against the sway.
Allow the combination to slow naturally.
Only apply brakes gently once swaying reduces.;

note right
  Common causes of snaking:
  — Speed too high for conditions
  — Load positioned too far to rear of trailer
  — Insufficient vertical load (Stützlast) on tow ball
  — Strong crosswind or gust from passing truck
  — Tyre blowout on trailer
  — Worn or damaged trailer tyres
end note

stop

legend right
  ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  LICENCE CLASSES AT A GLANCE
  ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  Class B:    Vehicle ≤ 3,500 kg | Trailer ≤ 750 kg OR combined ≤ 3,500 kg
  Class B96:  Vehicle ≤ 3,500 kg | Combined 3,500 kg to 4,250 kg
  Class BE:   Vehicle ≤ 3,500 kg | Trailer ≤ 3,500 kg | Combined ≤ 7,000 kg
  ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  SPEED LIMITS (Urban / Rural / Autobahn)
  ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  Towing vehicle ≤ 3.5 t, no Tempo-100:            50 /  80 /  80 km/h
  Towing vehicle ≤ 3.5 t, with Tempo-100:          50 /  80 / 100 km/h
  Towing vehicle > 3.5 t with trailer:             50 /  60 /  80 km/h
  Tempo-100 only applies on Autobahn / Kraftfahrstraße — NOT rural Bundesstraße
  ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  TEMPO-100 WEIGHT RATIOS (max trailer = car empty weight × factor)
  ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  Unbraked / braked without shock absorbers:        × 0.3  — NOT Tempo-100
  Braked + shock absorbers:                         × 1.1  — Tempo-100 eligible
  Caravan + shock absorbers + anti-sway coupling:   × 1.2  — Tempo-100 eligible
  Tempo-100 sticker must be visible inside the vehicle
  ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  VERTICAL LOAD — Stützlast
  ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  The downward force of the trailer drawbar pressing on the tow ball
  Too much → overloads rear axle — impairs steering and braking
  Too little → trailer snakes and sways dangerously
  Correct range → found in Zulassungsbescheinigung Teil I and owner's manual
  Typical value: 25–100 kg depending on vehicle
  ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  LOAD DISTRIBUTION IN TRAILER
  ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  Place heavy items: LOW and FORWARD (over or just ahead of the axle)
  Target weight split: 60% front / 40% rear
  Ensures correct Stützlast on tow ball
  Prevents trailer snaking
  (See also: stvo_trailer_flowchart.puml for full load compliance rules)
  ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  UNBRAKED vs BRAKED TRAILERS
  ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  Unbraked trailer: maximum permissible weight = 750 kg
  Braked trailer (Auflaufbremse / overrun brake): higher limit — see documents
  Overrun brake: activates automatically when car decelerates
  (trailer pushes forward into coupling → activates trailer brakes)
  ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  DOCUMENTS — Where to find vehicle-specific trailer data
  ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  Zulassungsbescheinigung Teil I: must carry in car — officially approved data
  Zulassungsbescheinigung Teil II: ownership document — kept at home (NOT in car)
  Owner's manual (Fahrzeughandbuch): manufacturer specifications
  Trailer has its own Zulassungsbescheinigung — must also be carried
  ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  COUPLING SAFETY CHECKS (before every departure)
  ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  1. Tow ball coupling locked — check indicator (green = locked)
  2. Safety chain / break-away cable connected
  3. Brake connection line connected (braked trailers)
  4. Lighting cable connected — walk around and check ALL lights:
     indicators, brake lights, rear lights, number plate light
  5. Trailer tyres: correct pressure and legal tread depth
  6. Load secured and within permitted limits
  7. Number plate on trailer: visible, clean, and lit at night
  8. Trailer handbrake released before moving
  ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  LIGHTING REQUIREMENTS ON TRAILER
  ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  Required: rear lights, brake lights, indicators, rear reflectors
  Rear fog light: required if trailer obscures car's rear fog light
  Number plate light: required
  Side marker lights: required on trailers over 6 metres long
  ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  PASSENGERS IN TRAILER
  ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  STRICTLY FORBIDDEN — no passengers may travel inside a trailer
  Applies even if the trailer is enclosed or fitted with seats
  ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  REVERSING WITH TRAILER
  ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  Steer in the OPPOSITE direction to where the trailer should go
  Use small, gentle steering inputs — trailer amplifies corrections
  Reverse slowly — have a second person guide where possible
  ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  FOLLOWING DISTANCE RULE
  ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  Combination > 7 m: minimum 50 m gap from vehicle ahead
  Only on roads outside built-up areas with one lane per direction
  Gap must be at the FRONT of your combination — for overtakers to pull in
  ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
endlegend

@enduml
